cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Bohrin in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Bohrin: an open standard for checking the graders of reinforcement-learning environments"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Bohrin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prabhu-gopal/bohrin"
url: "https://bohrin.com"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
abstract: >-
  Bohrin tests the graders of reinforcement-learning environments: the verifiers, reward
  functions and test suites that decide whether a model's work counts. It constructs
  submissions a correct grader must reject, each wrong by construction, and reports what a
  grader accepted as a Coverage Score and a Verification Gap with their uncertainty. A
  submission is called wrong only when that is established without asking the grader under
  test.
keywords:
  - reward hacking
  - reinforcement learning
  - RL environments
  - RLVR
  - verifiers
  - graders
  - evaluation
  - mutation testing
